# Without this the whole tree goes to the daemon on every build — measured at
# 1.35 GB and over five minutes just to transfer, before a single layer runs.
# The Dockerfiles install dependencies themselves and copy only what they name,
# so none of this is needed in the context.

# Rust build output. 836 MB on its own once the proxy has been built natively.
target/
crates/*/target/

# Installed by pnpm inside the image from the lockfile.
#
# `**/` and not just `*/`: the workspace packages live at artifacts/<name>/ and
# lib/<name>/, so their node_modules are two levels down and `*/node_modules/`
# never matched them. They were copied into the image by `COPY . .`, and pnpm
# then found a modules directory built by a different install on a different
# machine, decided it had to be purged, and aborted because a docker build has
# no TTY to ask.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# History is never read by a build.
.git/
.github/

# Local state and secrets — a .env in the context can end up in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/
*.log

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Test and coverage output.
coverage/
.nyc_output/
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/

# Build artefacts that are regenerated inside the image.
dist/
**/dist/

# Build-info files must go with the dist they describe.
#
# These record what a composite project last emitted. Copying one in while
# excluding the dist/ it refers to makes tsc conclude the output is already up
# to date and emit nothing — so lib/db and lib/api-zod produced no declaration
# files in the image, and api-server's typecheck failed with 72 TS6305
# "has not been built" errors. Nothing noticed before 2026-08-21 because the
# bundler reads TypeScript source directly and never needed the declarations.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.cache/
